1
00:00:00,930 --> 00:00:04,690
We've received word that Claw,
the esper terrorist organization,

2
00:00:04,690 --> 00:00:07,350
has barricaded itself
in the Seasoning Cultural Tower.

3
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:10,250
It's possible that they might also
be holding Prime Minister Yabe,

4
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:12,990
who was abducted from
Pork Bone City, prisoner insid—

5
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:15,780
The kidnapper was a teleporter.

6
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:18,200
He had the ability to instantly travel
wherever he wanted.

7
00:00:18,590 --> 00:00:22,510
And, according to the news, he can
also predict people's movements.

8
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,550
Well, that's not really fair.

9
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:28,210
How can one person have
two overpowered abilities like that?

10
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:31,880
Did you end up with a high fever
because of your opponent's ability?

11
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:34,680
No, this is just from the shock of losing.

12
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:37,480
I also got a fever when I lost to Kageyama-kun

13
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:39,390
and had nightmares for three days and nights.

14
00:00:39,390 --> 00:00:41,110
This guy sounds like bad news.

15
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:43,600
Do you think they have more like him?

16
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:47,300
I was always confident
I could take anyone on.

17
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:50,890
But now... I don't know what to think.

18
00:00:55,590 --> 00:00:58,450
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

19
00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:01,260
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

20
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:04,110
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

21
00:01:04,110 --> 00:01:05,170
(Get ready!)

22
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:10,760
Coming down, could you fill your satisfaction?

23
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:16,500
You're a MOB. Can't you feel your own frustration?

24
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:22,250
Coming down, could you fill your satisfaction?

25
00:01:23,270 --> 00:01:26,810
You're a MOB. What do you want to be?

26
00:01:26,810 --> 00:01:33,350
Wear your overflowing emotions on your sleeve and break it down.

27
00:01:34,570 --> 00:01:38,250
What do you see once you go beyond your limits?

28
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:41,230
(99.9! 99.9!)

29
00:01:41,230 --> 00:01:44,110
The mysterious percentage.

30
00:01:45,790 --> 00:01:48,580
Cryin' my life, cryin' my psyche,

31
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:51,530
cryin' my heart in such commonplaces!

32
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:54,360
Is that your ideal? Is that your mind?

33
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:57,270
It all begins when it hits 100.

34
00:01:57,270 --> 00:02:00,060
The MOB is alive. The MOB is high.

35
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:02,950
The MOB is staying frustrated, aren't you?

36
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:07,340
Is that your ideal? Is that your mind? Right now...

37
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:09,880
Your life is your own.

38
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:12,650
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

39
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:17,160
Mob Psycho

40
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:15,540
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

41
00:02:15,540 --> 00:02:18,410
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

42
00:02:18,410 --> 00:02:19,720
(Get ready!)

43
00:02:21,990 --> 00:02:27,000
Collision
~Power Type~

44
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:30,000
Why did we move away from the capital?

45
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,010
We could've just taken over
the tallest building in Japan.

46
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,710
There are two reasons.

47
00:02:35,950 --> 00:02:39,700
The first reason is the omurice
in the cafeteria here is to die for.

48
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:42,180
They use four eggs per serving.

49
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:45,980
The other reason is I'm from this city.

50
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:49,390
I know this city so well,
I can keenly monitor its changes.

51
00:02:49,390 --> 00:02:51,670
So this place is memorable to you?

52
00:02:51,670 --> 00:02:55,250
Maybe your old friends still live here.

53
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:59,400
Old friends and memories, huh?
I can't think of any.

54
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:01,610
I actually don't mind if you destroy it all.

55
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:04,580
Really? Even though you
remember the omurice?

56
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:06,690
Correct.

57
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:11,000
The special anti-terrorism squad has arrived.

58
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,500
We will now raid the Cultural Tower.

59
00:03:13,650 --> 00:03:15,320
Should I go?

60
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,710
There's no need.

61
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:21,430
Every soldier from Claw HQ is plenty capable.

62
00:03:21,430 --> 00:03:25,690
They aren't much inferior to
the upper echelon, the Scars.

63
00:03:23,090 --> 00:03:25,890
LP Gas

64
00:03:29,350 --> 00:03:33,360
Most of those guys are
artificial espers, aren't they?

65
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:36,020
When'd they become so strong?

66
00:03:36,190 --> 00:03:38,440
These guys aren't human...

67
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,740
Hey, boss. Just out of curiosity...

68
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,700
Did you do something to them?

69
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:56,960
A news helicopter, huh?

70
00:03:57,930 --> 00:04:00,920
You're a pain. Go away.

71
00:04:01,990 --> 00:04:03,450
The controls aren't working!

72
00:04:03,450 --> 00:04:04,390
A malfunction?!

73
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,850
I'm not sure! It's gone out of control!

74
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:09,810
That's one big RC helicopter!

75
00:04:09,810 --> 00:04:13,770
Leave the fighter jets
and missiles to Hatori.

76
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:18,180
I'll have Minegishi and Shibata go out
into the town to expand our territory.

77
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:21,070
Serizawa and Shimazaki
will defend this base.

78
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:24,660
We're going to show them
just how powerful we are.

79
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:25,410
Go!

80
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:28,740
No...

81
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:30,910
What is this?

82
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:33,590
We can't do anything about this...

83
00:04:33,590 --> 00:04:35,310
What are we going to do, Reigen?

84
00:04:36,670 --> 00:04:39,630
Hey! This is no time to be
eating cup noodles!

85
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:42,060
Don't act like this ain't
none of your business!

86
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:44,380
What are you talking about?
Of course it's not.

87
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:45,450
Huh?

88
00:04:45,450 --> 00:04:48,880
We're not superheroes, and this is dangerous.

89
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:52,070
It's best that we leave this
to the police and JSDF.

90
00:04:52,070 --> 00:04:53,850
What? Are you chickening out?

91
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:57,580
What do you think we can even do
against people like that?

92
00:04:57,990 --> 00:04:59,330
Well...

93
00:04:59,330 --> 00:05:02,570
We all gathered here to
ask you that, you dumbass.

94
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:05,240
Then, here's my answer...

95
00:05:06,110 --> 00:05:07,190
Meeting's over.

96
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:10,030
I thought we might have a chance with Mob,

97
00:05:10,210 --> 00:05:11,640
but this is just too dangerous.

98
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:14,270
We'll have to lie low until things blow over.

99
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:16,310
Reigen-san...

100
00:05:16,970 --> 00:05:19,250
I think that's the right decision.

101
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:23,710
I'm going. I'd rather make the first move
than be on the run forever.

102
00:05:23,710 --> 00:05:25,150
I'm going, too!

103
00:05:25,150 --> 00:05:25,920
Same!

104
00:05:26,230 --> 00:05:30,800
This battle is our chance to
find a purpose for ourselves.

105
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:31,890
Do whatever you want.

106
00:05:33,830 --> 00:05:36,960
Hello? Oh, you're calling
about the fire insurance...

107
00:05:37,450 --> 00:05:39,760
Yes, that's right...

108
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:44,070
Huh? If you can't figure out the cause,
there won't be any payout?

109
00:05:44,770 --> 00:05:46,450
You couldn't find any kerosene or gas?

110
00:05:46,450 --> 00:05:50,030
Of course not! It was caused by
psychic powers! Psychic powers!

111
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:52,590
You've never dealt with anything like this?
That's not my problem!

112
00:05:52,590 --> 00:05:54,600
Hey, wait a sec...

113
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,980
My office burned to the ground!
I'm penniless!

114
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:58,960
Why the hell do I even have insurance, then?

115
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,940
What the hell are you talking about?

116
00:06:00,940 --> 00:06:01,460
Hang on.

117
00:06:01,850 --> 00:06:04,820
Look at his face.
I've never seen him so serious before.

118
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:10,590
You guys are determined to fight, aren't you?

119
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,850
I've changed my mind.

120
00:06:12,850 --> 00:06:15,980
I'll command you all, just like you wanted!

121
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:17,010
We're gonna win!

122
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:21,020
And I'm gonna drag the damn arsonist
to the insurance company!

123
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:23,230
Master Reigen's all fired up!

124
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:25,440
Now that that's settled,
time to think up a strategy.

125
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:28,080
Get everyone a copy of the local map.

126
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:31,170
The enemy is apparently jamming
all electronic devices.

127
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:34,500
Looks like I was being a bit too negative.

128
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:42,210
You're pretty strong.
You probably didn't even need my help.

129
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:45,870
Ritsu, your latent abilities
far surpass your brother's.

130
00:06:45,870 --> 00:06:48,790
My abilities? There's no way that's true.

131
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:51,680
Life won't be any fun
if you don't tell yourself that.

132
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:54,930
The same goes for me.
I'm more powerful than my dad...

133
00:06:58,390 --> 00:07:02,010
As I figured, you really are
leading the uprising, Sho-kun.

134
00:07:02,010 --> 00:07:04,320
Talk about a textbook rebellious phase.

135
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:08,000
His aura is really peculiar. Who is that?

136
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,280
One of the Ultimate 5,
the highest echelon of Claw,

137
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,700
that's Minegishi the plant user.

138
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,810
Get caught by his plants, and you're finished.

139
00:07:14,810 --> 00:07:17,490
You get turned into plant food.

140
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:19,990
We'd be at a disadvantage if
we fought him in a forest,

141
00:07:19,990 --> 00:07:22,400
but too bad for him,
this is a concrete jungle.

142
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:24,810
We'll take care of him.

143
00:07:24,810 --> 00:07:26,900
Please go on ahead, leader.

144
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:28,900
You guys...

145
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:30,840
All right, Ritsu! Let's go!

146
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:33,780
I have my doubts.

147
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:37,350
Hey, look up in the sky!

148
00:07:38,660 --> 00:07:40,000
What's going on?

149
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,850
Are the government's espers attacking?

150
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,230
Shoot them down!

151
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:49,740
None of us are getting in those cars.

152
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:53,200
The first step in our plan is to
mess with the enemy formation.

153
00:07:53,530 --> 00:07:58,160
Try to buy us as much time as possible
before they realize it's a decoy.

154
00:07:58,160 --> 00:08:02,850
Um, Teru-san...
Is my telekinesis helping at all?

155
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:03,930
Yeah.

156
00:08:03,930 --> 00:08:07,880
It's like when someone uses their pinky
to help you carry some heavy luggage.

157
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:10,590
Can you even call that helping?

158
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:18,470
Damn it... I really can't do this alone!

159
00:08:18,470 --> 00:08:20,270
Would you like some help, young man?

160
00:08:20,270 --> 00:08:21,420
Who are you?

161
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:23,480
Oh, you decided to show up, too?

162
00:08:23,690 --> 00:08:25,760
My name is Takeuchi.

163
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:28,670
I am a master of the miraculous
art of super qigong.

164
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,640
You just need to make some cars fly, correct?

165
00:08:31,990 --> 00:08:34,430
What's happening on the surface
is merely a diversion.

166
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:38,160
We're going to infiltrate their main camp
through the sewers and defeat the boss.

167
00:08:40,810 --> 00:08:41,370
This way.

168
00:08:41,550 --> 00:08:45,950
Once they lose their leader,
none of them will be a threat individually.

169
00:08:54,090 --> 00:08:55,910
It's not just an ordinary paper fan?

170
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:58,930
It's been turned into a device
that amplifies shock waves.

171
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,390
Guys, get behind my shield!

172
00:09:04,390 --> 00:09:08,320
He disassembled and reassembled
the shredded vines and leaves?

173
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:09,860
That's an interesting technique.

174
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:15,530
I can even make a human-like doll from a
fridge as long as it has the right materials.

175
00:09:15,530 --> 00:09:16,690
You all right?

176
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:18,070
I'm fine.

177
00:09:18,070 --> 00:09:21,360
The other one's a rare healing type.

178
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:24,260
They're perfectly balanced in
attack, defense, and support.

179
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:28,080
I guess I should get a little serious.

180
00:09:31,410 --> 00:09:33,370
Should you really be here?

181
00:09:33,370 --> 00:09:35,410
What the hell am I supposed to do out there?

182
00:09:35,410 --> 00:09:37,600
Besides, when Mob wakes up,

183
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:40,850
it'll probably help if he has someone here
to explain the situation to him.

184
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:45,110
But man, he's really knocked out.

185
00:09:45,110 --> 00:09:47,730
He wouldn't be out so long
if he was just tired.

186
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:50,060
Master Reigen! There's trouble!

187
00:09:50,370 --> 00:09:53,010
Our security system picked up some intruders!

188
00:09:53,010 --> 00:09:54,030
Intruders?!

189
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:57,700
Claw? How'd they find this place?

190
00:09:57,980 --> 00:09:59,370
I'll lead you to the rear exit.

191
00:09:59,370 --> 00:10:01,590
No, it's no good to run off without a plan.

192
00:10:01,590 --> 00:10:02,610
We have to hide!

193
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,340
There's no doubt about it. They're in there.

194
00:10:18,090 --> 00:10:20,770
You guys shaking in your boots in there?

195
00:10:21,550 --> 00:10:23,760
Get your asses out here!

196
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,640
What do you want to do, Reigen?

197
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,980
Want me to possess you and brawl with them?

198
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,520
I'll open the door.

199
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:30,940
Stay on your guard.

200
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:38,550
You got me. I give up.

201
00:10:38,550 --> 00:10:40,420
I'm not an esper.

202
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:42,240
You can tell with your tracing powers, right?

203
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:47,040
This kid here is an esper, but he
hasn't woken up since last night.

204
00:10:47,430 --> 00:10:49,210
Let me take him to the hospital.

205
00:10:49,210 --> 00:10:52,890
This guy's pretty suspicious.
He might be packing a weapon.

206
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:54,610
Frisk them.

207
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:59,780
I don't have any weapons. I just have
my cellphone and a handkerchief.

208
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:01,920
This guy's got something
in his inside pocket.

209
00:11:02,270 --> 00:11:05,140
Oh, it's just some cologne.
I work in the service industry.

210
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:07,410
It's a great scent. See?

211
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:17,230
Apparently, it's filled with a curse
that causes extreme drowsiness.

212
00:11:17,950 --> 00:11:20,490
I confiscated it from four-eyes a while ago.

213
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:23,300
To think it'd actually come in handy here.

214
00:11:24,530 --> 00:11:27,180
I thought you were trash,
but you're not so bad.

215
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:30,250
You'll have to deal with me next.

216
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:31,710
He's huge!

217
00:11:31,710 --> 00:11:33,210
Here we go.

218
00:11:38,210 --> 00:11:40,720
He looked strong,
but thankfully he's also an idiot.

219
00:11:41,270 --> 00:11:43,800
Seriously, what's with this
ridiculous luck of yours?

220
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:46,120
You're definitely going
to die a horrible death.

221
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:52,980
Mob Psycho

222
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:56,480
Mob Psycho

223
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:59,740
What a splendid sight.

224
00:11:59,970 --> 00:12:04,450
We destroyed all that,
yet I don't feel a bit of remorse.

225
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:07,720
Sacrifices must be made in
the name of world domination.

226
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:09,200
Is that really true?

227
00:12:09,430 --> 00:12:11,970
Why the long face, Serizawa?

228
00:12:12,510 --> 00:12:14,890
Let me give you a word of advice.

229
00:12:14,890 --> 00:12:17,290
Yes, President! I'd love to hear it!

230
00:12:17,690 --> 00:12:21,160
The secret behind my undying positivity

231
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:24,800
is because I've never once
concerned myself with how others feel.

232
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:28,900
I've lived my life up till now
exactly how I wanted.

233
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:31,980
Everything will always work out
as long as I can count on myself.

234
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:37,230
I doubt my spirit will break
even if I ever lose all of you.

235
00:12:37,650 --> 00:12:41,450
I've decided to take over the world,
so I'll do so, even if it's by myself.

236
00:12:41,450 --> 00:12:43,250
Since I have the audacity to say that,

237
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:46,200
the world is basically already in my hands.

238
00:12:46,430 --> 00:12:50,790
Serizawa, I think very highly
of your potential.

239
00:12:51,710 --> 00:12:53,370
You held back on Joseph, didn't you?

240
00:12:54,810 --> 00:12:58,020
You need to obtain a unimpassioned,
audacious positivity.

241
00:12:58,020 --> 00:13:00,590
Then you can be just like me.

242
00:13:00,770 --> 00:13:03,800
I see! If I do my best,
I can be a corporate executive, too?

243
00:13:04,270 --> 00:13:06,800
Pretty sure his misunderstanding
has gotten even worse...

244
00:13:07,610 --> 00:13:09,790
First off, this isn't a company.

245
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:14,890
What now? They found out where we were!

246
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:17,330
First, we'll grab a taxi—

247
00:13:19,210 --> 00:13:20,040
Hey!

248
00:13:20,770 --> 00:13:22,990
What the hell? Weren't you sleeping?

249
00:13:22,990 --> 00:13:26,950
Looks like I've awakened
thanks to you, dumbass!

250
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:30,370
Right. Got it...
I seriously give up this time.

251
00:13:30,370 --> 00:13:31,410
If anything, we're—

252
00:13:31,410 --> 00:13:33,580
You idiot! Run, Reigen!

253
00:13:37,370 --> 00:13:38,180
Mob!

254
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:41,000
Psycho Steroid!

255
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:45,300
I frequently send psychic signals to
my muscles and continuously adjust—

256
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:47,760
Yeah, sure. Goodnight.

257
00:13:52,470 --> 00:13:53,840
Now he's lost his cool.

258
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:55,930
He's powered up even more!

259
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:58,920
I'm getting really sick of this,
but I'll lure him out!

260
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:02,010
He's not coming? Mob, wake up!

261
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:18,620
I panicked for a second,
but this guy's not an evil spirit.

262
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:19,560
He's human!

263
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:21,090
That means I can break him!

264
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:26,260
Okay, I retract that last statement.
This guy's not human.

265
00:14:26,730 --> 00:14:29,990
Shit! This isn't good! Catch him, Reigen!

266
00:14:29,990 --> 00:14:33,180
You got it! I once joined
the boys' volleyball team on a trial basis!

267
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:34,260
Just take it easy on me!

268
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:38,560
Dimple!

269
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:40,520
I-Is Mob's body okay?

270
00:14:41,650 --> 00:14:43,980
That was close... I think he's okay.

271
00:14:44,370 --> 00:14:46,440
It's all thanks to his shoe falling off.

272
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:48,730
But now I'm certain...

273
00:14:49,110 --> 00:14:51,160
I definitely can't win this fight!

274
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:53,620
Can't let that giant lug catch me!

275
00:15:00,730 --> 00:15:02,770
Uh... Are they going to be okay?

276
00:15:04,910 --> 00:15:08,580
The terrorist organization that has
taken over part of Seasoning City

277
00:15:08,580 --> 00:15:10,940
continues to wreak havoc across the city.

278
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:14,260
Citizens are being ordered to stay inside.

279
00:15:14,610 --> 00:15:15,640
You guys won't believe this!

280
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,100
Look!

281
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:20,310
Super Ultra Rare

282
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,310
I rolled a super ultra rare!

283
00:15:20,310 --> 00:15:21,070
For real?!

284
00:15:21,070 --> 00:15:22,000
Wow!

285
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,770
Inukawa, did you spend more mon—

286
00:15:25,730 --> 00:15:29,560
Fight on! Fight on! Fight on!

287
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:33,050
You can't go past here, even on foot.

288
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:34,240
MPD

289
00:15:33,050 --> 00:15:34,240
Haven't you seen the news?

290
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:36,080
What should we do, Captain?

291
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:37,790
Guess we'll just have to change our course.

292
00:15:37,790 --> 00:15:40,460
The same scenery all the time
gets boring anyway.

293
00:15:40,830 --> 00:15:44,420
Body improvement! Fight on! Fight—

294
00:15:45,270 --> 00:15:47,170
I knew something was off.

295
00:15:47,540 --> 00:15:49,880
I guess the cars in the sky
were a decoy after all.

296
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:53,190
Which means there's probably another group.

297
00:15:53,190 --> 00:15:55,600
Let's get some information out of them.

298
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:57,640
So many Scars...

299
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:59,350
But we have to do this.

300
00:15:59,350 --> 00:16:01,810
Hey, you're Terada.

301
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:05,020
You really did betray us, huh?

302
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:07,910
You're Ishihara, a Scar from the 4th Division.

303
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:10,030
What a rude accusation!

304
00:16:10,390 --> 00:16:13,950
I was acting as a spy
and gathering information.

305
00:16:13,950 --> 00:16:16,360
I can give you the information
you need on the enemy.

306
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:19,500
In return, let me join HQ's operation.

307
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:21,220
Terada-san!

308
00:16:21,220 --> 00:16:22,460
How could you?

309
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:23,880
This is a nightmare!

310
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:31,060
Did you actually think you had a chance
because there were three of you?

311
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:35,850
Never forget that the Ultimate 5 and
mere mortals are like night and day.

312
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:41,530
We're almost there.
If we keep going straight...

313
00:16:42,290 --> 00:16:43,540
Wait, stop!

314
00:16:44,790 --> 00:16:47,080
Something doesn't feel right up ahead...

315
00:16:47,510 --> 00:16:48,820
There's something there.

316
00:16:48,820 --> 00:16:49,550
What is it?

317
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:50,320
Here it comes!

318
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:58,040
Hello, Scars.

319
00:16:58,040 --> 00:17:02,550
I thought you were sewer rats since
you were scuttling around down here.

320
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:05,470
How unsightly.

321
00:17:05,910 --> 00:17:07,910
Let's end this here.

322
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:12,210
There's a crowd.

323
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:16,510
There's gonna be even more casualties,
but I'll just have to blend in and lose him.

324
00:17:17,250 --> 00:17:18,970
Whoa, that's amazing.

325
00:17:19,180 --> 00:17:21,420
Who is that guy? A pro wrestler?

326
00:17:20,090 --> 00:17:22,150
Hey, don't push!

327
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:22,930
He's sorta scary.

328
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,390
No way...

329
00:17:24,390 --> 00:17:26,330
That can't be...

330
00:17:26,900 --> 00:17:28,860
It's Tsubomi-chan!

331
00:17:29,670 --> 00:17:31,820
If something were to happen to Tsubomi-chan,

332
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:33,410
Shigeo would erase me!

333
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:35,530
I have to stop him!

334
00:17:38,490 --> 00:17:40,580
Full-power barrier!

335
00:17:44,830 --> 00:17:45,460
Huh?

336
00:17:46,470 --> 00:17:48,790
He hit so hard that
my possession came undone?

337
00:17:49,550 --> 00:17:52,030
What the hell?
A home run out of the park?!

338
00:17:52,030 --> 00:17:54,480
Wake up, Shigeo! Wake up!

339
00:18:07,010 --> 00:18:09,760
Why did Kageyama come falling from the sky?

340
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:12,570
Maybe someone was trying a long throw.

341
00:18:13,070 --> 00:18:14,920
I wonder who he is.

342
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:16,520
Those are some impressive muscles.

343
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:19,990
Were you the one who threw Kageyama?

344
00:18:20,810 --> 00:18:22,950
Kageyama is a member of our club.

345
00:18:22,950 --> 00:18:25,620
Whoever you are, I request
that you take your leave.

346
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:32,690
Captain!

347
00:18:32,690 --> 00:18:35,860
You bastard! Who the hell
do you think you are?!

348
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:38,510
I'll show you how much stronger I've gotten!

349
00:18:38,510 --> 00:18:40,260
Demon Rush!

350
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:41,850
Now it's our turn!

351
00:18:43,930 --> 00:18:45,720
Fight!

352
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:46,600
Onigawara!

353
00:18:51,310 --> 00:18:52,070
No way!

354
00:18:52,070 --> 00:18:53,770
With just one arm?!

355
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:24,260
I don't know what you have against him,

356
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:28,750
but he doesn't deserve to
have you step on his head!

357
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:30,730
Say, Kageyama...

358
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,650
That's right. You've worked so hard.

359
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:39,860
No matter how many times
you've passed out from anemia...

360
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:42,200
No matter how many times you've stumbled...

361
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:45,290
You've always been running right behind us.

362
00:19:45,290 --> 00:19:46,960
Just seeing you like that...

363
00:19:47,730 --> 00:19:52,660
...gives us courage!

364
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:57,110
That's not going to break
because of something like this!

365
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:07,600
I won't let you have Kageyama!

366
00:20:16,860 --> 00:20:19,280
That's Shigeo's senior for you.

367
00:20:19,990 --> 00:20:21,610
This guy's ripped!

368
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:24,220
Here we go! Unleashed!

369
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:26,870
Muscle Usage 100%

370
00:20:41,330 --> 00:20:43,290
What the hell are you so surprised about?

371
00:20:43,290 --> 00:20:46,010
Muscles built using psychic powers
don't stand a chance

372
00:20:46,010 --> 00:20:50,220
against muscles built by
training diligently every day.

373
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:52,510
This guy is way out of your league!

374
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:54,900
Shigeo was right.

375
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:11,250
Captain!

376
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:13,910
You're so awesome, Captain!

377
00:21:14,170 --> 00:21:17,460
Is that what they call an adrenaline rush?!

378
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:19,900
All that training paid off!

379
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:22,470
I-I did that?

380
00:21:22,470 --> 00:21:25,050
We need to celebrate your growth!

381
00:21:25,050 --> 00:21:27,840
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

382
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:30,310
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

383
00:21:30,310 --> 00:21:32,680
Shit! That guy's getting up again!

384
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:33,750
You can't be serious!

385
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:35,270
What should we do, Captain?!

386
00:21:35,270 --> 00:21:38,230
Actually... I haven't been able
to raise my arms for a while...

387
00:21:38,550 --> 00:21:40,540
I probably won't be able to do that again.

388
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:43,030
Here he comes!

389
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:50,410
Kageyama!

390
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:52,910
Everyone from the club?

391
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:55,720
Oh, whoops.

392
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:58,490
I guess I was sleeping.

393
00:22:01,420 --> 00:22:04,370
Make sure you don't fall asleep
outdoors again, Kageyama.

394
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:05,990
Sorry about that.

395
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:11,770
Dimple, what's going on right now?

396
00:22:16,320 --> 00:22:18,520
We're finally here.

397
00:22:18,930 --> 00:22:21,890
Just you wait, Dad!

398
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:41,710
I spilled a seed and lost sight of it

399
00:22:45,420 --> 00:22:50,720
I'll find it using the color it's dyed in and watch it grow

400
00:22:53,060 --> 00:22:59,190
It immediately returned to the palm of my hand

401
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:08,760
But it's still too light and too frail to reach for the skies

402
00:23:09,820 --> 00:23:14,380
The world coldly drains away all the heat

403
00:23:14,380 --> 00:23:18,930
The bright sunshine just isn't enough

404
00:23:18,930 --> 00:23:23,320
The memories are closing off what lies ahead

405
00:23:23,320 --> 00:23:28,420
Shake off their warmth and set off into the distance

406
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:35,180
If I let it wither, it'd be over just like that

407
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:40,470
But my hope just doesn't fade away

408
00:23:55,720 --> 00:23:58,080
After waking up,
Mob heads for Seasoning Cultural Tower.

409
00:23:58,310 --> 00:24:00,800
But he finds himself up against
Minegishi from the Ultimate 5!

410
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:03,280
Leave the strongest of
the Ultimate 5, Shimazaki, to me!

411
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:05,540
Next time on Mob Psycho 100 II Episode 11:

412
00:24:05,540 --> 00:24:06,920
"Guidance ~Psychic Sensor~."

413
00:24:06,920 --> 00:24:10,260
Guidance
~Psychic Sensor~

414
00:24:07,290 --> 00:24:09,840
Option B, the serious course, involves buying
the Blu-rays and the manga volumes.
